&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agile Robots&lt;/strong&gt; is a leading provider of AI-powered robotics solutions. By combining artificial intelligence and robotics, the company makes industries smarter, more flexible, and more efficient.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in Munich in 2018 by renowned robotics researchers from the German Aerospace Center (DLR), Agile Robots has experienced rapid global growth. Today, more than 3,500 highly skilled robotics and AI enthusiasts are employed worldwide. The company has one of the largest research and development teams in the AI and robotics industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agile Robots has built a unique portfolio; together with the subsidiaries BÄR Automation, Franka Robotics, idealworks, and Krause Automation, the company covers all areas of AI-driven robotics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more at: &lt;a id=&quot;menur58p&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;https://www.agile-robots.com/en/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://www.agile-robots.com/en/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin is the world’s leading platform for savings and investment products. Founded in 2012, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech&lt;/strong&gt; connects consumers with banks in the EU, the UK and the US. This gives consumers &lt;strong&gt;better interest rates&lt;/strong&gt; and banks a &lt;strong&gt;diversified form of refinancing&lt;/strong&gt;. Our vision is to offer savings and investments without barriers and thus open up the global 160 trillion euro market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin currently employs more than 800 people from over 75 countries worldwide. Today, the platform holds over 80 billion euros in assets from&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;more than one million investors&lt;/strong&gt; which have accrued over 5 billion euros in returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Raisin Group is scaling its Internal Audit function with a dedicated focus on Anti-Financial Crime (AFC). We are looking for a proactive expert to help build and mature this critical pillar of our governance framework. As a key member of our team, you will provide independent assurance, helping us navigate complex regulatory landscapes while driving operational excellence. If you are passionate about risk management and eager to shape the future of this young Group Internal Audit team, we invite you to join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct audits as per the annual audit plan. Experience in AML and other regulations combating financial crime and relevant standards and frameworks is highly appreciated. In addition, you will have the chance to develop and form the audit function within Raisin Group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance and Risk Assessment: &lt;/strong&gt;Evaluate the adequacy and effectiveness of controls, procedures, and systems to ensure compliance with statutory and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting and Recommendations: &lt;/strong&gt;Prepare detailed reports on audit findings, recommend improvements, and monitor the implementation of audit recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Engagement: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with various internal stakeholders, including risk management, and compliance teams, to ensure alignment on governance and compliance issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit Project Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage and coordinate internal and external audits, ensuring timely and thorough execution of audit plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Management reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare quarterly and annual reporting to Senior Management and presentations for relevant Committees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;appsElementsGenerativeaiAstList&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational Background: &lt;/strong&gt;Degree in Business Administration, Law, Economics, or a related field. Professional certifications such as CIA, CAMS, or equivalent are highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Minimum of 5+ years of experience in auditing, governance, risk, and compliance, ideally within the international financial services or FinTech industry. Proven experience in outsourcing/service provider management is a significant asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Knowledge: &lt;/strong&gt;Deep understanding of German financial regulations (BaFin, MaRisk) and EBA guidelines, with a specific, demonstrated focus on Anti-Financial Crime (AFC) frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interpersonal &amp;amp; Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Exceptional stakeholder management skills with the ability to bridge complex technical requirements and business interests effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Skills: &lt;/strong&gt;Professional fluency in English and German is required. Proficiency in other European languages is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join our mission, join our team – and grow with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Raisin, we care about each other and it is one of our top priorities to foster an open and caring environment in which everyone feels welcome and comfortable. Our culture is strongly driven by our ambitious team, which connects more than 75 different nationalities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our team, you will benefit from: &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Development Budget of €2,000 and four full training days per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours, home office and 30 vacation days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension scheme (Betriebliche Altersvorsorge), which we support with 20%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy more than 50+ different sports with Urban Sports Club: We subsidize your membership with more than €20 per month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you miss being in the office? The Deutschland Ticket gets you there, which we subsidize with €25 per month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love cycling? With JobRad, lease the bike of your choice and enjoy tax savings, plus Raisin covers your monthly insurance costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hungry all the time? Snacks, daily fresh fruit as well as drinks provided at the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are moving from another country or city to join us? We may support your relocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.raisin.com/corporate/raisin-applicant-privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Raisin Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;728&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;We value diversity and the unique experiences each individual brings. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;907&quot; data-end=&quot;1013&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for everyone, regardless of race, colour, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, or gender identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a leadership role spearheading Nebius’s communications across Europe and the Middle East: you will develop strong regional narratives, provide senior counsel, manage and develop the team, and lead consequential communications and stakeholder situations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reporting to the global Head of Communications, you will translate business priorities into compelling stories and a practical regional strategy. You will connect local developments to the company narrative and adapt them to the audiences and circumstances of each market.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We need an outstanding storyteller with the gravitas, experience and judgment to personally lead high-stakes situations involving multiple stakeholders. You will know when to shape the narrative, handle a difficult relationship or lead a response yourself, and when to give colleagues the authority and support to deliver.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The region has clear priorities, strong narratives, credible stories and trusted stakeholder relationships. Important situations receive the right senior attention. Colleagues understand their responsibilities, exercise sound judgment and develop under your leadership. Global colleagues have early visibility of consequential regional developments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Shape regional narratives and strategy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop communications strategy and strong narratives for priority European and Middle Eastern markets, linked to business priorities and the wider company story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify compelling stories and the evidence behind them. Make clear choices about audiences, markets and investment; adapt narratives locally while keeping core facts consistent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise senior leaders on positioning, communications opportunities and reputation risks. Define measurable objectives and use evidence to improve the programme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead communications and consequential stakeholder situations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with regional business leaders, partners and relevant business, technology, infrastructure and local media. Create a sustained pipeline of credible stories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape and deliver the narratives, writing, executive counsel and stakeholder engagement that need your senior experience. Delegate other work with clear briefs, authority and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional communications for customer, partner, product and infrastructure developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with country managers and public affairs colleagues on communications and local engagement around physical infrastructure builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage people and regional resources&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set team priorities and responsibilities, coach colleagues, manage performance and support their development. Build the capability and confidence to make sound decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance workloads and recommend where additional skills or capacity are needed. Recruit and onboard approved hires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct agencies and partners through clear briefs, budgets and performance reviews. Judge what to own personally, what to delegate and when to intervene; retain accountability for quality and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coordinate across the business&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with stakeholders across Nebius – GTM country leads, Marketing, Business Diplomacy, Product, Research, Technology, subject experts and other colleagues – to coordinate on issues including regional priorities, policy, local engagement and reputation management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with US, APAC and global communications leaders on announcements, issues and executive visibility. Maintain early visibility of consequential developments within appropriate confidentiality controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Qualifications and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;What we need&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong record of senior communications leadership in Europe and the Middle East, with substantial in-house technology-company experience and the ability to operate credibly across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding storytelling and narrative-development skills: translating complex business and technology priorities into compelling, credible stories for different audiences and markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated people-management experience: setting goals, coaching, managing performance and developing capable colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gravitas and senior experience to personally lead high-stakes, multi-stakeholder situations, advise business leaders and navigate competing interests with sound judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of judging when personal involvement is essential and when to delegate, alongside strong media relationships and experience directing agencies and regional resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding English writing, editing and spoken communication, with the curiosity and rigor to understand complex technology and build accurate narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Helpful experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI, cloud infrastructure, enterprise technology or another complex B2B sector; regional expansion, infrastructure investment or a publicly listed company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial Middle East communications work, relevant media relationships and additional regional language skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agency experience is valuable alongside substantial in-house experience; an agency-only background does not meet the role’s requirements. Journalism experience can be beneficial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competencies and Behavioural Traits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong narrative judgment, senior presence, clear prioritisation and calm leadership. A capable people manager who develops others, gives direct feedback and delegates with purpose. Takes personal ownership where the stakes or complexity require senior experience, while keeping regional and global colleagues aligned. Comfortable with ambiguity, iteration, course-correction, experimentation and (occasionally) failure.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A senior communications leadership role shaping narratives and stakeholder relationships across Europe and the Middle East, working closely with business and global communications leaders and developing the regional team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
